Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  09 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  09 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 08 50 CLINICAL DATA  Suture at deep margin                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3  TWO NODULES  2 5 CM AND REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO THE SUPERFICIAL MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN ALONG A BROAD FRONT AND TO LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE DEEP MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU IN THE REGION OF THE MASSES  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 15 47                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 15 09 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 7cm breast tissue with a suture designating the deep margin  The deep resection margin is inked black  and the superficial resection margin is inked blue  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a 2 5cm in maximal diameter pink gray  firm nodule that abuts the superficial resection margin and is deeply covered only by a thin rim of fibrous tissue  A second separate nodule  0 4cm in maximal diameter is also identified  A representative section of the large nodule in relation to both the superficial and deep resection margin is frozen as FX 1  now in cassette A  A representative section of the small nodule is frozen as FX 2  now in cassette G  Section code  A  large nodule  previously frozen as FX 1 B F large nodule  additional sections G  small nodule  previously frozen as FX 2 H  small nodule  entirely submitted I  grossly unremarkable breast parenchyma  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   LEFT BREAST LARGE NODULE   INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  SEE NOTE   FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2   LEFT BREAST  SMALL NODULE   INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , Absent.
