Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  08 MAY 01 ACCESSIONED ON  08 MAY 01 at 10 53 CLINICAL DATA  Ductal carcinoma in situ  right simple mastectomy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  SMALL FOCUS OF RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Invasion of the stroma  blood vessels  and lymphatic vessels is not seen  The margin of the specimen appears free of the ductal carcinoma in situ  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  16 MAY 01 at 07 15                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm right simple mastectomy oriented by a long suture designating the 12 o clock  The specimen bears a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm ellipse of skin remarkable for a REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm well healed scar on the superior aspect as well as an unremarkable nipple measuring 3 0cm in diameter  The specimen is black inked entirely and serially sectioned to reveal white fibrous and yellow lobulated fatty tissue  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A  tissue near nipple and anterior margin  B  inferior margin  C  deep margin  D E  representative sections  F  fibrous tissue  antero lateral  Resident  SOHEIL DADRAS  MD  PHD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  W P Andrew Lee  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY , Absent.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  10 REMOVED_MONTH 00 ACCESSIONED ON  10 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 11 23 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  CARCINOSARCOMA WITH FOCAL CARTILAGINOUS AND OSSEOUS DIFFERENTIATION  SEE NOTE   NOTE  The tumor is composed of both malignant epithelial and mesenchymal  sarcomatous  areas  These two components are distinct and do not show any merging from the carcinoma into the sarcoma  Immunoperoxidase stains confirm divergent differentiation  with cytokeratins being positive only in the epithelial areas and vimentin and desmin only in the sarcomatous regions  S 100 only stains the carcinoma  Although the differential diagnosis includes a metaplastic carcinoma with extensive sarcomatous areas  there is usually more blending of the epithelial and mesenchymal areas in metaplastic carcinoma  Also  immunoperoxidase usually shows some keratin positivity in the sarcomatous areas in a metaplastic carcinoma  Another interesting feature in this case is that the background of this tumor is reminiscent of a phylloides tumor  with broad stromal fronds focally covered by malignant epithelium  This feature raises the possibility that this tumor is arising in a high grade phylloides  All margins are greater than 0 2cm  No angiolymphatic invasion is seen  Dr  Koerner has reviewed the case and agrees with this interpretation  Diagnosis by  Jacqueline Haas  MD Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 13 15                                                                                     ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION Addendum     ADDENDUM  ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION   The tumor size is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm  see gross description   No lymph nodes were identified in the axillary tail  Sections taken from this region also do not reveal lymph nodes  Added by  Jacqueline Haas  MD Signed On  18 MAY 00 at 16 04 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right modified radical mastectomy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm right modified radical mastectomy with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 9 0cm tan wrinkled skin ellipse and a 2 9cm symmetrical nipple areolar complex  A short suture designates superior and long suture designates the axillary tail per the surgeon  There is a 5 5cm well healed curvilinear scar approximately 5 0cm lateral to the areola  The specimen is inked black and serial sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm well demarcated tan red  focally necrotic mass which comes within 2 7cm of the posterior margin of resection  closest margin  and approximately 0 5cm from the skin  Approximately 1 5cm superior posterior to the mass is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 7cm area of skin wedge  The posterior margin is retracted  Sectioning of this area reveals tan white fibrous tissue  A mass cannot grossly be identified in this area  The remaining breast tissue reveals approximately 65  yellow adipose tissue and 35  tan white unremarkable fibrous stroma  A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm axillary tail is present containing no definite lymph nodes  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A D  Tumor  E  Posterior resection margin adjacent to tumor  F  Posterior margin  area of retraction  G  Random breast tissue  H J  Possible lymph nodes from axillary tail  Gross Description by  DELIA FINNIE Resident  DANIELLE ELLIOTT  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Danielle D Elliott  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY , Absent.
